venv/

# Editor and OS droppings. Nobody's local setup belongs in a public dataset repo.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Source workbooks. `fetch_kato.py` holds the .xlsx in memory and never writes
# one, but its `--workbook <path>` flag invites downloading a copy into the tree.
# The workbook is 916 KB of binary that regenerates from a URL recorded in
# data/kato.source.json, so it is never the thing to commit — the CSV is.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.docx
*.rar

# dist/ is NOT ignored. GitHub Pages and jsDelivr serve it straight from the
# repository, so the generated artifacts are committed by design (SPEC.md §3).

# data/ is NOT ignored, and data/rates.csv least of all. It is the dataset —
# hand-curated, cited, and the entire point of the project.

# Fetched documents, keyed by id. Reproducible from the site, and the sha256
# that matters is recorded on every extracted row, so the bytes are not tracked.
.cache/

# Blind task files `scripts/validate_readings.py --emit` writes for the LLM
# validation gate. Regenerable from `.cache/documents/` (also gitignored) plus
# that script, and read by nothing else — committing them would mean tracking
# a derived artifact that a fresh clone must regenerate before `--ingest` can
# verify anything anyway (see the module docstring for what that means).
data/validation-tasks/

# Which documents the last `--emit` run could not fetch a task for. Same
# reasoning as validation-tasks/: a snapshot of the last run, not a source.
data/validation-unavailable.json

# ── Internal working files. Deliberately NOT published. ──────────────────────
# The agent process — roles, decisions, evidence, handoffs, the work queue — is
# how this repository was built, not what it publishes. A reader wants the
# parser, the tests and the data. A copy lives outside the repository, so
# removing these from git does not delete them — but it does mean they stop
# being backed up by pushing.
.claude/
.plans/

# Market sizing, revenue ceilings and build costs. Internal, and not the product.
docs/BUSINESS.md

# Agent orchestration glue: reads broker credentials from a local container and
# starts a session on this machine. Internal infrastructure, not part of the
# dataset or its pipeline.
scripts/trigger_reconcile.py
